      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The test verifies that `ByteOrderMark.UTF_32LE.getBytes()` returns the correct 4-byte sequence. The main understandability issues are:\n- `(byte)(-1)` / `(byte)(-2)` are opaque — BOM bytes are conventionally expressed in hex\n- Anonymous inline array in `assertArrayEquals` hides the semantic meaning\n- No explanation of what encoding is expected\n\nI'll write an improved version using hex literals and descriptive variable names.The improved test compiled successfully. The key changes made were replacing the opaque `(byte)(-1)` / `(byte)(-2)` literals with their hex equivalents `(byte)0xFF` / `(byte)0xFE`, naming the expected array `expectedUtf32leBytes`, and separating it from the assertion for clarity — all while preserving identical runtime behavior."
